# One line-ending policy for every host. The tree is LF today and the toolchain does not
# care either way (KickAssembler under Java, pwsh 7, Python and check-ascii.py all read
# either), so a CRLF round-trip through a Windows editor would be a whole-file diff for
# nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Data files are byte-exact and stay that way: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.anm binary
*.prg binary
*.bin binary
*.fnt binary
*.mus binary
*.pic binary
*.spr binary
*.bnr binary
*.bas binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
